WEBVTT

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.980
I won't let you kill Hibiki.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.210
Alcor!

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.540
The trial has ended.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.190
You should have no reason to appear.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:11.920
Yes, indeed.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.010
You have succeeded at
the trial of Polaris.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.450
But now, I shall begin
an attack of my own will.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.260
Your "will"?

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.680
That's strange talk for a Septentrion.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.460
The will that has sprouted
in me is not due to Polaris.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.440
A strange feeling, isn't it?

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.340
I will kill you and
entrust hope to Hibiki.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.060
Hope? To me?

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.530
Is that so? Well, fine.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.060
I'll do it... Alcor.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.070
Yes, Yamato. My...

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.500
first friend.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.930
The trial of Polaris...

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.700
Seven days of challenging
the gods has ended.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.900
The world can be remade by
those humans who have survived.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.590
Which is the right choice?

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:06.220
What did we hope to achieve by fighting?

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.290
What did we hope to gain?

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.510
We defeated the seven
Septentriones, right?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.420
What the heck? We're still not safe?!

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.030
The trial to test humanity is over.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.740
Now, the audience with
Polaris will begin.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.300
What... will happen?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.710
If Yamato has his way,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.820
the law of the world will be rewritten,

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.060
and a world of meritocracy begin.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.930
Forcibly?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.460
It'll be like the world
was always that way.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.590
I'm scared...

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.000
I don't want somethin' like that!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.740
That's why we have... to stop...

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.330
Hibiki! Hibiki!

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.830
Your power increases the
closer you get to the tower.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.900
I see. So, I was lured here?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.710
My connection to you ends today.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.400
In the end, I will teach
you the concept of death.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.250
I'm quite interested in that.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.400
But, sadly, it seems I
won't have the opportunity.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.120
Because I will kill you here and now.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.920
Then you'll entrust
Hibiki with a choice?

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.500
Yes. That's what I want.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.380
It's strange I've come to
think that way, isn't it?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.430
The Sparkling One, eh?

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.510
Yes. Through meeting him, I was changed.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.990
For the first time, I was a
person, not just some system.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.700
My heart now pounds over
a future I can't predict.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.580
It's thrilling.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.460
It's a delusion. Either
that, or you're broken.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.630
Oh, really?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.240
Even you, Yamato, have paid
Hibiki notice this whole time.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.720
Are you broken, too?

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:17.650
Neither my will nor my
intentions have changed.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.130
He's merely a part of my plans. A tool.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:26.880
Is that so? You speak like Polaris.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.280
Alcor.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.180
You are a system. Stop trying to think.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:36.020
If you do, I'll take you to the
future that will be remade.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:37.660
Yamato.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.770
The future you imagine is of
a world of choices denied.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.410
That doesn't make me happy.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.950
A friend's dead face clip has arrived.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.170
I see.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.230
I'll do it, Alcor.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.250
I will... kill you.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.440
Yamato's and Alcor's dead face clips.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.190
So, one of them will be right, huh?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.380
I have to go!

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.280
If you go now, you'll just get killed.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.230
What can you do against those monsters?!

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.160
I made a promise.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.770
I would stop Yamato.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.620
That's what I promised.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.040
You made that promise?!

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.030
It's the one thing that Yamato and I

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.540
exchanged that's been somewhat human.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.250
If I can't agree, I
should pass judgment.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:39.930
Makoto!

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.390
I... will help the bureau chief.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:45.350
What? No way!

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.890
You can't go help him, can you?!

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.650
Shijima. Nitta. Kuze.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.600
I've caused you much unpleasantness.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.610
I know I can't make up for that.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.980
It wasn't your fault, was it?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.350
You just carried out your orders.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.980
I don't know if that's
right or not, but...

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:09.110
Exactly. I don't know
if it's right or not.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:09.900
However...

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.270
No matter what happens to
me, I will follow the chief.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.160
That's what I've decided.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.250
So then... you loved him?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.290
You make it sound so foolish.

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:26.300
I'd lost faith in the world.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:31.300
Injury had put an end to my
life as an agent of the state,

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.300
but he gave me back the world
in the palm of my hand.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.670
The bureau chief gave
me a sense of purpose.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.020
Though, in living for his purpose,

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.150
I may have just been avoiding things.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.490
If there's a future that he wants,

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.440
then I want to make it happen.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.920
That's all.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.280
You have no doubts about
the future Yamato plans?!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.960
I had lost hope in the future.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:59.370
Then, Hotsuin took me in.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.820
From the start, I could
speak nothing of the future.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:07.810
But isn't that the end of thought,
which people have depended on?!

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:08.590
Hibiki!

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.060
That's going too far.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.480
You're right.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.940
All I can do is rely
on the hopes of others.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.370
I'm a weak human.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.190
And Yamato is hope?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.230
He is to me.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.660
Pallas Athena isn't ready yet?

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.770
A friend's dead face clip has arrived.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.570
Makoto!

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:38.140
The dead face clip can be avoided.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.540
That's what you've said, isn't it?

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.500
But it's reckless not to have a plan!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.240
Indeed.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.900
But I'd always been prepared
to throw down my life.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.630
If it's for his sake, I have no regrets.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:52.700
But that's just wrong!

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.340
You're quite intelligent.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:59.050
But it seems you don't understand.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.960
This is my final request:
Take care of the chief.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:05.980
Makoto!

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:18.700
That's such a cruel way to say it!

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:34.260
Yamato.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.750
Even for one who can wield
the power of Ryumyaku,

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.350
there are limits to the human body.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.100
It's time.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.580
Healing is complete.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:04.760
Cerberus!

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.670
Silence him.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:16.770
True to form, Yamato.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.180
To be expected of the
human I initially chose.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.180
Cerberus!

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:30.900
There are no demons you can
soon summon, are there?

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.530
The system that you made...

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.610
It determines the abilities of the user

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.280
and can summon the
appropriate demon, yes?

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.010
That's right.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.240
It's made so that more powerful demons

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.130
can be called to match
the user's growth.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.920
I see. Now that you've
defeated BeneTnasch...

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:54.920
I'll be using this!

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.230
I won't let you.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.640
Unfortunately, this
game with you is ended.

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:33.980
Sir.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:39.610
You've been my... reason for living.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.520
Thank you.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.110
Makoto.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.100
You fool.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.360
"Thank you," huh?

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.320
To her, you were hope.

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:01.770
Alcor.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.300
Nebiros! Zao Gongeng!

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.500
Could be I'm at a disadvantage.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:50.500
How long as it been since
we've had such fun, Yamato?

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:51.980
Fun?

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:55.210
I've never once thought
that, being with you.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:59.670
Really? Those words sadden me the most.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:03.560
You've said that you're an
observer of human civilization.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.300
I just played with you.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:09.270
I see. You were kind and played with me?

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:10.930
Thank you.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:15.810
I'll ask you, now, at the end:
Why did you follow me so?

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.080
Because you're intriguing.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.570
When you were young, I thought
you were the Sparkling One.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.820
But I wasn't this "Sparkling
One" of which you speak.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:33.590
Yamato, the path you're
trying to take is...

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.140
Pitch black.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.010
Could be.

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.260
Have you not once amended your thinking?

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.690
There's no need for me to stop.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:46.810
The world was already
corrupt when I was born.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:49.880
The inept may avert their eyes,

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.100
but human society is past help.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.620
Someone must enact change.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:59.480
And I'm the only one who can do it.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.730
Things can be lost through
brute force, yes?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.620
Irrelevant.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.110
I said I would shoulder that sin myself.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:08.710
Yamato.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:12.990
Why do you seek to bear everything
on such small shoulders?

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:17.210
The human heart is not
made that way, is it?

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:19.150
Shut your mouth.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:22.840
You were born with
extraordinary abilities.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.600
Being different from normal children,

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.750
you bore the responsibility
of the transcendent,

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.510
were bound by restrictions.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.000
That's why you're so interesting.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:35.680
And I came to like you.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.940
Shut up. I win.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.220
Yes, indeed.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:45.690
But if I don't stop you,
you will kill Hibiki.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:51.510
Bastard!

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.580
I'm sorry, Yamato.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.130
I've broken you, haven't I?

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.090
What are you talking about?

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:13.730
I'm the one who's made
you this way, Hotsuin.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:19.750
I though it for the best, but
it's ended up driving you mad.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:21.530
Yamato.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.110
I've enjoyed the time
we've spent together.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:26.970
Oh, really?

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:29.500
Anyone who'd feel joy
over this is a child.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.610
I'll play with you again.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:33.720
I understand now.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.450
I thought for sure that, together,

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.370
we could go toward a splendid future.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.840
Yamato. Somehow, in the new world...

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.130
Alcor!

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.130
You plan to kill us both?

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:54.570
Yamato.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.360
Yamato! Alcor!

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.390
Goodbye.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.070
Stop it!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:28.270
Alcor. Yamato.

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:30.230
THIS is the trial?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.700
I've had enough!

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:36.920
Are you satisfied, Polaris?!

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.560
So you've come to stop me, Hibiki?

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.000
Yamato!

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.070
Where's Alcor? Where's Makoto?

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:56.070
Fools.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:58.910
They're dead?

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.380
Yes. I killed them.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:07.710
Your decision... You
have to go that far?!

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.130
Yes.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:14.170
It has begun. The change.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.630
The world will be broken!

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:26.940
To be reformed, to be rewritten
will take but an instant.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.320
The gate shall appear.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:38.320
The Transport Terminal.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:42.980
It's time to choose.
I shall go to Polaris.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:43.700
Yamato!

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:48.100
It's thanks to you all that
we defeated all our enemies.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.290
I'm grateful.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.970
You made them run amok on purpose?

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:01.240
If you're going to stop me, then come.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.350
If you have the strength to defeat them.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.480
Yamato!

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.410
The physical limit has been reached.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:14.940
Has it been protected?

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:20.520
Goodbye, Hibiki Kuze.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.730
Hee ho!

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:35.130
Hibiki!

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:36.520
Hibiki!

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.190
Daichi! Nitta!

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.200
Hibiki! What's going on here?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.610
Yamato went to meet Polaris.

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.740
So then, Alcor...

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:48.850
No way!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.650
H-He's a Septentrion, right?!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:54.410
That's how powerful Yamato is.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:59.790
It's no good. I can't
follow that monster!

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.800
Monster, huh?

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:07.450
Lugh!

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:18.340
Hibiki, we'll handle
things here somehow.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.480
Right, Nitta?

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.820
Yes. Don't worry.

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.720
We've survived these seven
days, so we're tough!

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:28.160
I can't leave you!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.950
Who knows what kind of obstacles

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.310
there'll be when the world is reformed.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.610
We have to stay together!

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:37.440
I wish we could together.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.610
But it looks like that's
far from certain.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:42.710
Also, we can't stop him.

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:43.740
Hibiki!

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:47.780
The seven days we fought
weren't in vain.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:50.870
I mean, you remained till the end!

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.840
Go, Hibiki! You're the hope of us all!

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:05.960
Byakko!

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.860
Hee ho!

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:36.470
Daichi! Nitta!

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:38.090
Stay back, Hibiki!

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:39.550
Please, go!

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:56.900
I'm sure the world will
turn out how he wants.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.930
That'll be good, right?

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:04.020
Yeah. Hibiki's smarter
than us. It'll be fine.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.420
Yeah.

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:06.410
Huh?

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.810
Who is Hibiki again? It's like...

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:14.580
my memories... are fading.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:18.810
Yeah. Everything is disappear--

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:25.600
But he... I remember he was a friend.

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:29.990
But why did this happen to us?

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:33.780
Huh? Who am I?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:38.270
It's kinda like... I'm
suddenly super anxious.

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:56.660
Yamato!

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.430
Hibiki.

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:03.420
Nitta and Daichi both
disappeared. Now...

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:06.290
The world is just you and me.

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:07.840
I see.

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:11.780
I thought you wouldn't arrive
at Polaris' side, but...

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:12.560
Somehow, you have.

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:16.310
It seems audience will not be granted
till I settle things with you.

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:19.000
That is the judgment.

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:22.570
Yamato, I'll keep my promise.

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:23.860
Promise?

00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:27.820
That I'll beat you and have
audience with Polaris!

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:30.800
It seems you have no more hesitation.

00:22:31.210 --> 00:22:35.080
Yes, that's good. Hibiki!

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:36.460
Cerberus!

00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:40.540
Byakko!
